# ─── Internal working notes — not part of the public source tree ───────────
# Unanchored on purpose: an `internal/` folder is private wherever it appears
# (docs/internal/, backend/internal/, FunctionPacks/**/internal/ …), matching
# the project's "internal stays internal" posture.
#
# The one carve-out is `frontend/app/internal/`. That is a Next.js ROUTE
# SEGMENT, not a notes folder — the ignore rule hid it from git, so no review,
# hook, or CI diff ever saw it, while `next build` compiled it from the working
# tree and served it publicly. Re-including it needs both lines: git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so the directory has to
# be un-ignored before its contents can be.
internal/
Internal/
!frontend/app/internal/
!frontend/app/internal/**

# ─── FunctionPacks — public pack library (sources + bundled reference data) ───
!FunctionPacks/
!FunctionPacks/**
FunctionPacks/**/INTERNAL_NOTES.md
# `!FunctionPacks/**` above re-includes everything under this tree, which
# would defeat the global `internal/` rule — re-assert it here.
FunctionPacks/**/internal/
FunctionPacks/**/Internal/
FunctionPacks/dist/
FunctionPacks/**/__pycache__/
FunctionPacks/**/*.pyc
FunctionPacks/**/*.egg-info/
FunctionPacks/**/.DS_Store
